Sec. 30001 amends the Consumer Financial Protection Act of 2010 to reduce the annual funding cap for the Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection from 12 percent to 6.5 percent of the Federal Reserve System’s total operating expenses. This change significantly limits the Bureau's available budget by halving the percentage of Federal Reserve funds it can access. The amendment specifically targets section 1017(a)(2)(A)(iii) of the Act to enforce this stricter financial constraint on the agency.

Sec. 30002 rescinds all unobligated balances of funds previously made available for the Green and Resilient Retrofit Program for Multifamily Housing under the Inflation Reduction Act of 2022. This action effectively cancels remaining financial resources designated for this specific housing retrofit initiative. The provision ensures that no further obligations can be made against these specific appropriated amounts.

Sec. 30003 eliminates the Securities and Exchange Commission Reserve Fund by striking subsection (i) of Section 4 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 and transferring all remaining obligated and unobligated balances to the general fund of the Treasury effective October 1, 2025. The SEC may only expend previously obligated amounts for ongoing programs until that date, after which the Fund is closed and unavailable for any purpose. The whistleblower awards fund is modified to remain available without further appropriation or fiscal year limitation, but the broader Reserve Fund is dissolved. This change removes the SEC's independent reserve mechanism and consolidates its remaining assets into the Treasury.

Sec. 30004 appropriates $1,000,000,000 for fiscal year 2025 to carry out the Defense Production Act, with funds remaining available until September 30, 2027. This new appropriation is in addition to amounts otherwise available and is drawn from funds not otherwise appropriated. The funding supports the implementation of the Defense Production Act (50 U.S.C. 4501 et seq.) during this specified period. [end of text]


